    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to present No. 5 Parkhill Road to the market, a spacious three-bedroom end-of-terrace family home ideally positioned within the ever-popular and mature residential setting of Kilnamanagh. Occupying a large corner site, this property offers generous outdoor space and excellent potential for future extension to the side, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nVacant and ready for immediate occupation, the property has been freshly painted throughout and benefits from some upgraded flooring, creating a bright and well-presented living environment. The accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming hallway, spacious living room, open-plan dining room and kitchen. Upstairs, there are three generously proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The property is heated by oil-fired central heating (OFCH).\n\nExternally, the property benefits from an exceptionally generous corner site. To the front, there is off-street parking together with a large front garden and a sizeable green area directly opposite the property. To the side, the substantial garden provides excellent potential for a future extension, subject to the necessary planning permission. The property also enjoys a private sunny rear garden, providing an ideal space for family activities, entertaining and gardening. A block-built shed provides valuable additional storage.\n\nKilnamanagh is a highly regarded residential area, renowned for its strong community atmosphere and excellent range of local amenities. No. 5 is within easy reach of Kilnamanagh National School, local shops and services, while an extensive selection of further amenities can be found nearby in Tallaght and Clondalkin. The property also benefits from excellent transport links, with the M50, N7, N81 and Belgard Road all easily accessible. Public transport is well catered for, with nearby Luas and Dublin Bus services providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the generous accommodation, exceptional corner site and excellent potential this property has to offer."
      },
